# =============================================================================
# West Chester Preschool — repo-wide gitignore
# =============================================================================
# The deployable Astro app lives in site/ ; the Sanity Studio will live in
# studio/ (added later). Generic folder patterns below match at any depth, so
# they cover site/node_modules, site/dist, etc. without per-folder entries.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Dependencies & build output (any subfolder) ----------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
.astro/
.wrangler/
.output/
.sanity/

# Generated idempotency cache written by the migration scripts (local-only:
# maps a local image path -> its uploaded Sanity asset id so re-runs skip
# re-uploading). CI never runs the migrations, and Sanity dedupes assets by
# hash anyway, so this must NOT be tracked. Tracking it broke `prettier --check`
# every time a migration reformatted it. See site/scripts/pagebuilder-lib.mjs.
# No leading slash -> matches this basename at any depth (i.e. under site/).
.asset-map.json

# Sanity typegen intermediate (2026-08-27). `npm run typegen` extracts the
# Studio schema to site/schema.json, then generates the COMMITTED types at
# site/src/lib/sanity.types.ts. Only the types are tracked: schema.json is a
# large machine artifact that adds nothing a reviewer can read.
schema.json

# Directory migration (scripts/migrate-directory.mjs): photo-URL -> Sanity asset
# id cache, and the temp ES module it writes while parsing the family code block
# (which holds real PII). Local-only, never commit.
.dir-photos.json
.families.tmp.mjs

# ---- Secrets — keep API keys and tokens out of the repo ---------------------
# .env.example / .dev.vars.example ARE committed as templates for new setups.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev.vars*
!.dev.vars.example

# =============================================================================
# FAMILY PII — NEVER COMMIT
# =============================================================================
# These reference files contain REAL family names, home addresses, phone
# numbers and emails (a hardcoded FAMILIES array + new-family additions + the
# class rotas). They stay on disk as migration reference, but must never enter
# git history. In the new stack this data lives ONLY in Sanity, behind the
# family-hub gate — see the migration plan. Do not remove these lines.
# =============================================================================
directory-additions-2026-2027.txt
wcp-directory-block.html
wcp-family-map.html
WCP_Rota_*.xlsx
.~lock.*#

# ---- The rest of the root migration workspace (belt & suspenders) -----------
# The repo tracks the deployable app (site/) + config only. The project root
# also holds the Squarespace migration workspace: ALL the family-hub code
# blocks (directory, co-op jobs, HEALTH/EMERGENCY, fundraising, budget,
# tuition), the class rotas/rosters, and the proposed budget. These hold real
# family names, children's health/emergency info, and finances. Local only —
# in the new stack this data lives ONLY in Sanity behind the family-hub gate.
/wcp-*.html
/*.pdf
/*.xlsx
/WCP_Project_Extraction.md
/code-injection.md
/P-01-global.css
/fonts/

# ---- Editor / OS noise ------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
~$*
.claude/settings.local.json

# ---- Media harvested from the old Squarespace site --------------------------
# Staging area for photos/videos/logos pulled from the live site. Kept out of
# git: real media belongs in Sanity, and any child photos shouldn't sit in the
# repo. Curate from here, then upload the keepers to Sanity.
assets-from-squarespace/

# Compressed hero video — 8.9MB, belongs in Sanity/R2 in production, not git.
# The tiny WebP poster IS committed (it's the LCP fallback).
site/public/hero/*.mp4
site/public/hero/*.webm

# ---- Lighthouse / Playwright / audit artifacts ------------------------------
.lighthouse*/
phase-*.png
.playwright-mcp/
playwright-report/
test-results/
playwright/.cache/
# Saved Family Hub session from tests/hub-auth.setup.ts — a real signed-in
# cookie for whatever password .dev.vars holds. Never commit it.
site/tests/.auth/
/backups/
